From 693dfaac6a79c25eca3c710eb2fffdb5b0044eb1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lakr233 <git@qaq.wiki>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:05:56 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 72/76] vgpu: read macOS 27's object descriptors

Component: object-list descriptor decode (all pathways).

At protocol 237 a macOS 27 guest's serializer writes TextureDescriptor2
records, and object-list descriptors embed the record their object was
made from. Read with the 32-byte layout, the 40-byte descriptor gave
formats like 0x500 (the pixel format's high byte beside usage's low
byte) and widths like 0x80000000, and every render target, type-11
surface and memoryless texture was refused.

read_descriptor now gives each descriptor the shape protocol 62 gives
the same object before anything decodes it:
- type 9 is a 0x34 record, rewritten as record 1;
- type 11 is a mapping prefix and a 0x39 record, rewritten as 0x2f;
- types 2 and 3 end in a 0x34 record, rewritten in place.
The 0x37 and 0x38 records already have wide decoders and are left alone.

Two more object forms appear at that protocol:
- Object type 19 is a buffer carved from a resource pool, with the
  buffer descriptor's trailing four zero bytes dropped. The list entry
  reports it as a buffer and the descriptor is padded.
- Compute pipeline descriptors carry tag 0x08,
  maxTotalThreadsPerThreadgroup (1024 on every record seen). It is a cap
  on dispatches this device sizes from the dispatch record, so it joins
  the benign tags instead of refusing the pipeline.

Measured on arm64 Linux (NVIDIA GB10), macOS 27.2 guest at protocol 237:
the descriptors in the tests are ones that boot sent.

Verified:
- cargo test -p reims-vgpu --no-default-features
  --features backend-vulkan,host-window -- --test-threads=1 passes,
  with five new tests over the captured descriptors.
- clippy reports the same 40 diagnostics as before.

Not verified: the backend-metal and x86 arms.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
